<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Spring bids mostly firmer.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Spring bids mostly firmer.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring bids were mostly firmer on Wednesday as farmer selling stalled in parts of Minnesota and Montana, merchandisers said.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures settled mixed with March up one cent to end at $3.89-1/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;We are taking in grain but it was mostly soybeans,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said. The dealer noted no movement in wheat. &quot;Farmers are waiting for higher prices.&quot;</p>
<p>A Montana merchandiser said he bought 40,000 bushels of winter wheat on Tuesday but just a few small loads on Wednesday,</p>
